    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0241" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/519: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-18T23:00:00+01:00">March 18, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 18—7:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1298. I duly informed Sir Alexander Cadogan in the sense of the Department’s
                    instruction No. 1034, March 11, midnight. He tells me that he is awaiting a
                    report which was requested from Sir Reader Bullard<anchor n="3" xml:id="d246-f1"
                    /> following my earlier conversation with him, (my telegram No. 1050, March 5, 7
                    p.m.). He assures me, however, that the Foreign Office “unreservedly welcome the
                    principle of Anglo-United States cooperation in Persian questions” and fully
                    share the view that such cooperation is the best means of strengthening the
                    position in Persia to the advantage of the cause of the Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d246-f1" n="3" xml:id="d246-f1-content">
                <p>British Minister in Iran.</p>
            </note>
